1
00:00:00,720 --> 00:00:53,860
Full of Surprises

2
00:00:53,860 --> 00:00:54,770
Don't tell me.

3
00:00:54,770 --> 00:00:56,760
Please don't tell me.

4
00:00:56,760 --> 00:00:58,340
I recognize you ...

5
00:00:58,340 --> 00:00:59,790
Oh, don't be silly, Arnie.

6
00:00:59,790 --> 00:01:01,200
Of course you recognize him.

7
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:03,650
Except for the beard, he hasn't changed in fifty years.

8
00:01:03,650 --> 00:01:04,830
It's Malcolm Stewart!

9
00:01:04,830 --> 00:01:06,650
I know it's Malcolm Stewart.

10
00:01:06,650 --> 00:01:10,170
You haven't changed much in fifty years.

11
00:01:10,170 --> 00:01:12,960
Peggy--Peggy Pendleton!

12
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:14,920
You're Peggy Pendleton!

13
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:16,460
Who am I, you old rascal?

14
00:01:16,460 --> 00:01:18,040
You don't recognize me, do you?

15
00:01:18,040 --> 00:01:19,860
I know who you are.

16
00:01:19,860 --> 00:01:23,080
You're Arnold Franklin!

17
00:01:23,080 --> 00:01:25,820
I know who you are!

18
00:01:25,820 --> 00:01:31,830
You look wonderful, Malcolm!

19
00:01:31,830 --> 00:01:34,750
Sit down. Sit down.

20
00:01:34,750 --> 00:01:35,620
Pete isn't home.

21
00:01:35,620 --> 00:01:38,000
Really?

22
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,050
No. He left a note on the door

23
00:01:40,050 --> 00:01:42,470
saying he was going to the railroad station

24
00:01:42,470 --> 00:01:44,510
to pick up a surprise.

25
00:01:44,510 --> 00:01:45,610
He's so funny.

26
00:01:45,610 --> 00:01:47,130
Always full of surprises,

27
00:01:47,130 --> 00:01:50,000
even fifty years later.

28
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,160
The two of you look unbelievable!

29
00:01:53,160 --> 00:01:54,630
How's your family?

30
00:01:54,630 --> 00:01:55,600
Oh, I was sorry

31
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:57,970
to hear about your wife having passed away.

32
00:01:57,970 --> 00:02:00,100
Yes. About four years ago.

33
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:02,910
And you're living with your children now? In New York?

34
00:02:02,910 --> 00:02:04,170
Pete wrote us and told us.

35
00:02:04,170 --> 00:02:05,140
Yup.

36
00:02:05,140 --> 00:02:09,290
Retired and moved to New York

37
00:02:09,290 --> 00:02:11,760
to live with my son and his family.

38
00:02:11,760 --> 00:02:12,770
By the way,

39
00:02:12,770 --> 00:02:15,400
what do you think this big surprise is?

40
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:19,920
It could be most anything, knowing Pete.

41
00:02:19,920 --> 00:02:22,970
Hey, that must be Pete!

42
00:02:22,970 --> 00:02:28,320
Now we'll find out about the surprise.

43
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:29,790
So good to see you all!

44
00:02:29,790 --> 00:02:32,100
Oh, Pete, Pete!

45
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:36,150
Oh, it's so good to see you!

46
00:02:36,150 --> 00:02:37,630
Remember Lillian?

47
00:02:37,630 --> 00:02:39,080
I remember all of you.

48
00:02:39,080 --> 00:02:40,710
You haven't changed a bit.

49
00:02:40,710 --> 00:02:44,310
Lillian! Oh, my gosh! Lillian

50
00:02:44,310 --> 00:02:45,870
Lillian Winters. Lillian Winters

51
00:02:45,870 --> 00:02:48,030
We were together in the Thursday night drama society.

52
00:02:48,030 --> 00:02:49,910
Remember me, Malcolm?

53
00:02:49,910 --> 00:02:52,160
Oh, beautiful as ever, Lillian.

54
00:02:52,160 --> 00:02:54,360
How's Donald? Donald

55
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:56,140
That's OK, Malcolm.

56
00:02:56,140 --> 00:02:58,620
Donald passed away a couple of years ago.

57
00:02:58,620 --> 00:03:00,790
Sorry to hear that, Lillian.

58
00:03:00,790 --> 00:03:01,420
Oh, I'm so sorry.

59
00:03:01,420 --> 00:03:02,990
I would not have missed this get-together for the world!

60
00:03:02,990 --> 00:03:04,860
And your little surprise, Pete?

61
00:03:04,860 --> 00:03:06,160
You really surprised me

62
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:08,990
by having us all come together.

63
00:03:08,990 --> 00:03:12,780
You don't know what the surprise is yet?

64
00:03:12,780 --> 00:03:14,500
Come on!

65
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:21,840
We'll tell you the big surprise.

66
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:25,090
I've invited you here for the weekend to help celebrate.

67
00:03:25,090 --> 00:03:26,210
Celebrate?

68
00:03:26,210 --> 00:03:27,600
Our fiftieth reunion?

69
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:28,440
No.

70
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:30,310
No. Pete wants to tell you ...

71
00:03:30,310 --> 00:03:32,930
Now, let me have the honor, Lillian.

72
00:03:32,930 --> 00:03:34,850
For goodness' sake, Pete, tell us!

73
00:03:34,850 --> 00:03:37,720
I can't wait much longer.

74
00:03:37,720 --> 00:03:41,230
Well, I am pouring this iced tea

75
00:03:41,230 --> 00:03:45,700
so that we can toast Lillian--and me.

76
00:03:45,700 --> 00:03:48,290
You don't mean to tell me that you and ...

77
00:03:48,290 --> 00:03:50,340
Yes, I do.

78
00:03:50,340 --> 00:03:53,490
I have loved Lillian all these years,

79
00:03:53,490 --> 00:03:58,240
so I asked her to be Mrs. Pete Waters.

80
00:03:58,240 --> 00:04:00,170
And I said yes.

81
00:04:00,170 --> 00:04:02,730
I knew it! I knew it!

82
00:04:02,730 --> 00:04:04,460
Congratulations!

83
00:04:04,460 --> 00:04:04,910
Oh, Lillian,

84
00:04:04,910 --> 00:04:06,910
I am so happy for you both.

85
00:04:06,910 --> 00:04:08,410
It's wonderful!

86
00:04:08,410 --> 00:04:10,220
It's wonderful for me.

87
00:04:10,220 --> 00:04:13,800
Lillian will make me a happy man--finally.

88
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:17,030
You are full of surprises, Pete.

89
00:04:17,030 --> 00:04:17,900
We are going to

90
00:04:17,900 --> 00:04:22,550
spend the entire weekend having a good time together here

91
00:04:22,550 --> 00:04:23,490
on the farm.

92
00:04:23,490 --> 00:04:26,490
We are going to celebrate all weekend.

93
00:04:26,490 --> 00:04:28,960
When is the wedding?

94
00:04:28,960 --> 00:04:30,770
That's another surprise.

95
00:04:30,770 --> 00:04:35,260
Lillian and I were married two weeks ago in Detroit.

96
00:04:35,260 --> 00:04:37,290
She's come here to stay.

97
00:04:37,290 --> 00:04:39,200
Wait till I tell my family about this!

98
00:04:39,200 --> 00:04:42,200
Why, that's wonderful!
